The invention relates to a method for producing and deburring toothed profiles on workpieces (6), utilizing two workpiece spindles (3, 3′), a hobbing tool (12), and a deburring device (10), wherein the workpieces (6) are automatically clamped into the workpiece spindles (3, 3′), and are subsequently toothed by means of the hobbing tool (12) before being deburred. The method comprises the following steps:

a. receiving an unmachined workpiece (6) at a first loading position (19) via a first workpiece spindle (3) and transporting said workpiece (6) to the hobbing tool (12);

b. performing a mill cut;

c. depositing the workpiece (6) at the first loading position (19) and receiving a further unmachined workpiece (6);

d. transporting the workpiece (6), having undergone the mill cut, to a second loading position (19′);

e. receiving the workpiece (6) at the second loading position (19′) via a second workpiece spindle (3′) and transporting said workpiece (6) to the deburring tool (10);

f. deburring the workpiece (6),

wherein an intermediate storage (14) for at least one workpiece (6) is provided between the first loading position (19) and the second loading position (19′), wherein the workpiece (6) is transferred from the intermediate storage (14) to the second loading position (19′), and wherein method steps e. and f. are carried out concurrently with method step b.

