# Patent Claim: Simultaneous Hobbing and Deburring Transport System

## Claim 1

A method for transporting and machining workpieces in a gear manufacturing system, comprising:

**a)** providing a first machining station configured to perform a hobbing operation on a workpiece at a first spindle loading position, and a second machining station configured to perform a deburring operation on a workpiece at a second spindle loading position, said first and second machining stations being operatively coupled via a workpiece transport mechanism;

**b)** providing an intermediate storage buffer disposed between the first spindle loading position and the second spindle loading position, the intermediate storage buffer being configured to temporarily hold at least one workpiece independently of the operational state of either the first machining station or the second machining station;

**c)** loading a first workpiece onto the first spindle loading position and performing a hobbing operation thereon to produce a hobbed workpiece;

**d)** transferring a previously hobbed workpiece from the intermediate storage buffer to the second spindle loading position and performing a deburring operation thereon, said deburring operation being carried out **simultaneously** with the hobbing operation of step c);

**e)** upon completion of the hobbing operation of step c), transferring the hobbed workpiece from the first spindle loading position to the intermediate storage buffer, thereby replenishing the intermediate storage buffer for a subsequent transfer cycle;

**f)** upon completion of the deburring operation of step d), removing the deburred workpiece from the second spindle loading position and transporting said deburred workpiece to a downstream processing or unloading station;

**g)** repeating steps c) through f) in a cyclical sequence such that the hobbing operation at the first spindle loading position and the deburring operation at the second spindle loading position are performed concurrently for each successive workpiece, the intermediate storage buffer decoupling the cycle time of the hobbing operation from the cycle time of the deburring operation;

wherein the transport mechanism comprises at least one workpiece gripper or shuttle configured to selectively transfer workpieces between the first spindle loading position, the intermediate storage buffer, and the second spindle loading position without requiring direct transfer between the first and second spindle loading positions.

## Claim 2 (Dependent)

The method of claim 1, wherein the intermediate storage buffer is configured to hold a plurality of workpieces sequentially, thereby permitting a variable dwell time for each workpiece between completion of the hobbing operation and initiation of the deburring operation.

## Claim 3 (Dependent)

The method of claim 1, wherein the transport mechanism comprises a pick-and-place unit having at least two gripper elements, a first gripper element configured to transfer workpieces between the first spindle loading position and the intermediate storage buffer, and a second gripper element configured to transfer workpieces between the intermediate storage buffer and the second spindle loading position.

## Claim 4 (Dependent)

The method of claim 1, further comprising synchronizing the cyclical sequence via a control unit configured to monitor completion signals from the first machining station and the second machining station and to initiate transfer operations in response thereto, such that the intermediate storage buffer maintains at least one workpiece available for transfer to the second spindle loading position at all times during steady-state operation.

## Claim 5 (Dependent)

The method of claim 1, wherein the hobbing operation and the deburring operation have differing cycle times, and wherein the intermediate storage buffer compensates for the difference in cycle times to maintain continuous, uninterrupted operation of both the first machining station and the second machining station.

# Patent Claim

**Claim 1**

The invention relates to a gear hobbing and deburring machine comprising:

a machine bed;

a first work spindle arranged on the machine bed and configured to hold and rotationally drive a workpiece during a hobbing process for generating a toothed gear profile on the workpiece;

a second work spindle arranged on the machine bed and configured to hold and rotationally drive the workpiece during a deburring process for removing burrs formed on the toothed gear profile of the workpiece;

a hobbing tool assigned to the first work spindle for performing the hobbing process;

a deburring tool assigned to the second work spindle for performing the deburring process;

a workpiece handling device configured to transfer workpieces between a loading station, the first work spindle, an intermediate storage unit, and the second work spindle;

**characterized in that**

the intermediate storage unit is arranged between the first work spindle and the second work spindle and is configured to temporarily receive and hold at least one workpiece that has undergone the hobbing process at the first work spindle, such that the hobbing process performed on a subsequent workpiece at the first work spindle and the deburring process performed on a preceding workpiece at the second work spindle are executable in an overlapping, time-parallel manner, independently of a cycle time of the respective other process,

wherein the workpiece handling device is configured to remove a hobbed workpiece from the first work spindle and deposit it into the intermediate storage unit while the second work spindle is still performing the deburring process on a previously stored workpiece, and to subsequently transfer a workpiece from the intermediate storage unit to the second work spindle upon completion of the deburring process, thereby decoupling the cycle times of the hobbing process and the deburring process from one another and increasing the overall throughput of the machine.

---

**Claim 2** (dependent)

The gear hobbing and deburring machine according to claim 1, wherein the intermediate storage unit comprises a plurality of workpiece receiving positions such that a plurality of hobbed workpieces awaiting the deburring process can be buffered simultaneously.

**Claim 3** (dependent)

The gear hobbing and deburring machine according to claim 1 or 2, wherein the workpiece handling device comprises a robot, a gripper, or a pick-and-place unit movable between the first work spindle, the intermediate storage unit, and the second work spindle.

**Claim 4** (dependent)

The gear hobbing and deburring machine according to any one of claims 1 to 3, further comprising a control unit configured to control the workpiece handling device based on a completion status of the hobbing process at the first work spindle and the deburring process at the second work spindle, so as to coordinate transfer of workpieces to and from the intermediate storage unit and thereby maximize overlap between the hobbing process and the deburring process.
